// =====================================================================================
// cedsEmbedTextGates — the CEDS round trip's text-node positive-exclusion conjunct
// =====================================================================================
//
// PHASE P5 of the forge embed-text revision (embedText-091426; PLAN §8.1 R-ET-5, §8.3 R-ET-20).
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT IN cedsFidelityGates.jsonc (R-ET-34, RADIANT_QUEST 2026-09-14): that file is
// also read by the LIVE `graphBuilder -cedsGates` action (apps/graph-builder/lib/actions.js),
// whose measures come from roundTripGateMeasures.js. A conjunct measured only by a hermetic
// test would read UNMEASURED there forever, and a gate that can never pass live teaches readers
// to skip the live suite. This file is read ONLY by forges/ceds/test/test-cedsRoundTrip.js,
// which is where the measure is actually produced, over REAL rows through the REAL compiler,
// canonicalizer and diff. (test-cedsGates.js synthesizes its measurements from each gate's own
// expectation, so a gate read there could never be red on real data.)
//
// WHAT THE CONJUNCT PROVES, STATED EXACTLY: a DmeEmbedText node and an EMBEDS_TEXT_OF edge fed
// into the in-test reader double — whose selection step mirrors roundTripCompiler.js:837-846
// (the role list) and :877-891 (the role-scoped edge queries) — leave the emission unchanged.
// It proves THE DIFF: that a text node reaching emission WOULD move inventedTotal (the twin's
// data-level observation) and that the mirrored allowlist keeps it out. It does NOT prove the
// production Cypher allowlist; that is proven only by P7's live run (inventedTotal 0).
//
// Same vocabulary as cedsFidelityGates.jsonc, evaluated by lib/roundTripGates.js. The twin lives
// in test/cedsEmbedTextGateTwins.js, not lib/roundTripGateTwins.js: the fidelity registry is
// audited for orphans against the fidelity file (test-cedsGates.js), and a twin declared here
// would read there as an orphan.
{
  "suiteName": "cedsEmbedText",
  "suiteVersion": "1.0.0",
  "acceptanceRule": "every gate PASS and every twin observed RED. No percentage participates.",

  "gates": [
    {
      "id": "E-1", "family": "E",
      "contract": "A text node and its EMBEDS_TEXT_OF edge are excluded from the round trip: with them present, inventedTotal is 0, lostTotal EQUALS the run without them, and the emitted RDF and its canonical statement set are byte-identical to that run.",
      "note": "The data-level red is observed in test-cedsRoundTrip.js: the same conjunct computed over a run whose selection double admits DmeEmbedText as a class goes false, with inventedTotal recorded.",
      "measure": "probe:embedTextExcludedFromEmission", "comparator": "equals", "expected": true,
      "twin": "admitEmbedTextRole"
    }
  ]
}
